```
     1→# UI/UX Revamp Plan — Kspec Web UI
     2→
     3→**Task:** @01KJXQK4
     4→**Status:** Active
     5→**Date:** 2026-03-04
     6→
     7→---
     8→
     9→## 0. Development Workflow
    10→
    11→All UI revamp work happens in an **isolated clone** of the repo on a long-lived feature branch. This prevents in-progress UI work from affecting the main working copy.
    12→
    13→### Setup
    14→
    15→```bash
    16→# Clone to a separate directory
    17→git clone /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui
    18→cd /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui
    19→
    20→# Create the feature branch
    21→git checkout -b feat/ui-revamp
    22→
    23→# Bootstrap
    24→node scripts/bootstrap.cjs
    25→
    26→# Initialize kspec (creates .kspec/ worktree pointing to same kspec-meta branch)
    27→kspec init
    28→```
    29→
    30→### Work Rules
    31→
    32→1. **All code changes** happen in `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui` on `feat/ui-revamp`
    33→2. **Task tracking** uses kspec from either location — both share the same `kspec-meta` shadow branch
    34→3. **Commits** go to `feat/ui-revamp` with conventional commit format + task trailers
    35→4. **Periodic rebases** from `main` to stay current: `git fetch origin main && git rebase origin/main`
    36→5. **Sub-branches** for individual tasks branch off `feat/ui-revamp`: `git checkout -b feat/ui-revamp/phase-1-tokens`
    37→6. **PRs** target `main` from the feature branch (or sub-branches for smaller merges)
    38→7. **Daemon API changes** that are prerequisites should be PRed to `main` first, then rebased into the UI branch
    39→
    40→### Directory Layout
    41→
    42→```
    43→~/Projects/
    44→├── kynetic-spec/           # Main working copy (main branch, day-to-day work)
    45→│   └── .kspec/             # Shadow branch (kspec-meta) — shared state
    46→└── kynetic-spec-ui/        # UI revamp clone (feat/ui-revamp branch)
    47→    └── .kspec/             # Same shadow branch — tasks visible from both
    48→```
    49→
    50→### When to Merge
    51→
    52→Each phase produces a mergeable increment. PR to `main` when:
    53→- Phase deliverable is complete
    54→- All E2E tests pass
    55→- Existing functionality is preserved (progressive enhancement)
    56→- No regressions in current views
    57→
    58→---
    59→
    60→## 1. Vision & Goals
    61→
    62→Transform the kspec web UI from a functional but basic dashboard into a polished, comprehensive interface that:
    63→
    64→- Exposes **all** kspec features through intuitive navigation
    65→- Provides real-time visibility into agent work (dispatch, sessions, streaming output)
    66→- Uses a kanban-style task dashboard with active work prominence
    67→- Delivers a professional, non-"AI slop" design built from imgen's proven design system
    68→- Supports both power users (keyboard navigation, command palette) and casual viewing
    69→
    70→### Non-Goals
    71→- Drag-and-drop kanban (tasks transition via agents/CLI, not manual dragging)
    72→- Mobile-first design (desktop primary, responsive secondary)
    73→- Replacing the CLI (UI complements CLI, doesn't replace it)
    74→
    75→---
    76→
    77→## 2. Design System: Porting from imgen
    78→
    79→### 2.1 Token Architecture
    80→
    81→Port imgen's `token-contract.css` to establish the foundation:
    82→
    83→```
    84→design-bg, design-fg, design-surface, design-border
    85→design-primary, design-accent, design-muted
    86→design-ring (focus), design-radius, design-shadow
    87→```
    88→
    89→**Color space:** oklch() for perceptual uniformity and wide gamut support.
    90→
    91→**Dark theme baseline (from imgen Design 27/28):**
    92→- Background: `oklch(0.12-0.15 0.01 250)` — deep blue-charcoal
    93→- Surface: `oklch(0.16-0.20 0.01 250)` — card/panel backgrounds
    94→- Border: `oklch(0.24-0.26 0.015 250)` — subtle dividers
    95→- Primary: `oklch(0.58 0.22 25)` — signal red (or adapt to kspec brand)
    96→- Accent: `oklch(0.7 0.2 145)` — green for success/active states
    97→- Muted text: `oklch(0.55 0.02 60)` — secondary content
    98→
    99→**Status color mapping (from kynetic-internal, adapted to oklch):**
   100→
   101→| Status | Color token | Usage |
   102→|--------|------------|-------|
   103→| pending | amber | Waiting, queued |
   104→| in_progress | orange | Active work |
   105→| pending_review | blue | Review needed |
   106→| needs_work | yellow | Fix cycle |
   107→| completed | emerald | Done |
   108→| blocked | red | Cannot proceed |
   109→| cancelled | zinc/gray | Archived |
   110→
   111→### 2.2 Typography
   112→
   113→From imgen's system:
   114→- **3 font families** via CSS custom properties (primary, secondary, mono)
   115→- **Fluid sizing** with `clamp()` for headlines
   116→- **Eyebrow text:** `0.75rem`, uppercase, `letter-spacing: 0.08em`, accent color
   117→- **Headlines:** `clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem)`, tight tracking (`-0.02em`)
   118→- **Body:** `0.875-1rem`, `line-height: 1.5-1.6`
   119→- **Mono** (for ULIDs, code, agent output): system mono or JetBrains Mono
   120→
   121→### 2.3 Component Naming
   122→
   123→Follow imgen's `ds-` prefix convention:
   124→- `.ds-card`, `.ds-badge`, `.ds-button`, `.ds-input`
   125→- Status variants via data attributes: `[data-status="in_progress"]`
   126→- All components scoped to avoid leaking
   127→
   128→### 2.4 Animations & Motion
   129→
   130→Port from imgen:
   131→- **Breathing/pulse** for active agent work (`.ds-gen-breathe`)
   132→- **Shimmer** for loading skeletons
   133→- **Entrance animations** with stagger for list items (blur + translateY)
   134→- **All gated** behind `prefers-reduced-motion`
   135→
   136→---
   137→
   138→## 3. Information Architecture
   139→
   140→### 3.1 Navigation Structure
   141→
   142→```
   143→┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   144→│ [Logo] kspec          [Search ⌘K]  [Connection] │
   145→├──────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┤
   146→│ Sidebar  │                                      │
   147→│          │  Main Content Area                   │
   148→│ Dashboard│                                      │
   149→│ Tasks    │                                      │
   150→│ Specs    │                                      │
   151→│ Agents   │                                      │
   152→│ Sessions │                                      │
   153→│ Inbox    │                                      │
   154→│ Observe  │                                      │
   155→│ Triage   │                                      │
   156→│ Plans    │                                      │
   157→│ ──────── │                                      │
   158→│ Validate │                                      │
   159→│ Search   │                                      │
   160→│ Settings │                                      │
   161→└──────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘
   162→```
   163→
   164→**Sidebar:** Collapsible icon rail (like kynetic-internal's ProjectSidebar). Each section has an icon + label. Badge counts for actionable items (inbox count, unresolved observations, pending review tasks).
   165→
   166→**Header:** Project name, command palette trigger, connection status indicator, project selector (multi-project).
   167→
   168→### 3.2 Page Hierarchy
   169→
   170→```
   171→/                      → Dashboard (overview)
   172→/tasks                 → Task board (kanban)
   173→/tasks?ref=@slug       → Task board with detail modal open
   174→/specs                 → Spec tree browser
   175→/specs?ref=@slug       → Spec tree with detail panel
   176→/agents                → Agent definitions + dispatch status
   177→/agents/dispatch       → Live dispatch view
   178→/sessions              → Session history list
   179→/sessions/:id          → Session detail (chat log)
   180→/inbox                 → Inbox items
   181→/observations          → Observations (friction/success/question/idea)
   182→/triage                → Triage workflow
   183→/plans                 → Plan records
   184→/validate              → Validation results + alignment
   185→/search                → Dedicated search (also via ⌘K)
   186→```
   187→
